      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(control-ui): import Codex and Claude Code memory",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw operators can migrate coding-assistant configuration from the CLI, but the Control UI had no reviewed way to discover and import Codex consolidated memory or Claude Code auto-memory into a selected agent workspace.\n\nCloses #106215\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds additive `migrations.memory.plan` and `migrations.memory.apply` Gateway methods plus provider-owned Codex and Claude Code memory discovery. Plans are agent-scoped, memory-only, fingerprinted, and rebuilt before apply. Exact item selection, workspace-bounded no-follow writes, no-clobber replacement staging, verified pre-import backups, item backups, reports, and recovery metadata keep the web flow reviewable and recoverable.\n\nThe Codex source contract was checked directly: consolidated memory reads `MEMORY.md` and `memory_summary.md` ([reader](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/2f7d89b1419bf7064346855b0acde23514b1ebc5/codex-rs/memories/read/src/lib.rs#L13-L14)), with the files documented as the durable memory artifact and generated summary ([memory docs](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/2f7d89b1419bf7064346855b0acde23514b1ebc5/codex-rs/memories/README.md#L96-L100), [reader behavior](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/2f7d89b1419bf7064346855b0acde23514b1ebc5/codex-rs/memories/README.md#L136-L137)).\n\n## User Impact\n\nSettings now includes **Import Memory**. Operators can select an agent, preview Codex and Claude Code memory collections without exposing file contents to the browser, choose exact files, import them, and explicitly replace existing imports after a refreshed conflict preview. Imported files live under the selected workspace's `memory/imports/` tree; source memory remains unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head `d2689b7ba00e0722be168dd06a85274944b6a77a`: 161 focused tests passed across 8 Vitest shards for Gateway protocol/handlers, provider discovery/apply, exact selection, restrictive fs-safe replacement/recovery, navigation, and the new page ([Testbox run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29271108871)).\n- Remote `pnpm check:changed` and `pnpm build` passed after the final code fixes: generated surfaces, all core/UI/extension typechecks, lint fan-out, security/database/architecture guards, plugin SDK surface/API verification, production bundles, precompressed assets, and Control UI performance budgets. The final main rebase was rechecked with 20 clean Control UI locales with zero fallbacks, 21 clean native locale artifacts, and the exact-head focused suite.\n- Live Control UI proof on this macOS machine with real local Codex and Claude Code memory: imported 2 Codex files and a selective 4-file Claude collection, refreshed conflicts, exercised replacement, verified the pre-import archive plus item backups/recovery reports, and byte-compared Codex source/destination files. No real workspace was mutated; proof used an isolated temporary workspace.\n- Behavior-validator black-box contract: 5 passed, 0 failed, 0 blocked.\n- Autoreview: clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
